    "whoFor": "**A good fit:**\n\n- Machine and equipment builders designing assemblies with many moving and bought-out parts\n- Fabrication and sheet-metal firms that need accurate drawings for the shop\n- Product engineering teams that must hand drawings to suppliers and customers\n- Companies that already work in DWG and want a drawing-led path into 3D\n\n**Probably not the right buy:**\n\n- A start-up designing a consumer product that needs CAD, CAM and electronics in one place; look at [Fusion](/products/fusion-360)\n- A one-person workshop that only needs occasional 3D models\n- A team that only draws in 2D; [AutoCAD](/products/autocad) is a simpler purchase\n\nA frequent mistake is to buy the heaviest tool because it sounds serious. Match the tool to the output you hand to the shop floor.",
